  "subdivision_of_building": "The application site is located at the ground floor, occupying the corner unit at the junction of Seven Sisters Road and Green Lanes",
  "status": "Approved",
  "description": "Installation of Internal Kitchen Ventilation System within existing cafe Unit",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;The kitchen extraction system, including its maintenance, must be installed and permanently maintained in accordance with the approved details set out in &#x27;Kitchen Extraction System Report &amp;amp; Odour Risk Assessment July 2025&#x27; and plans titled &quot;316 Green Lanes Kitchen Ventilation Plan&quot; (Project No. 2506098, Drawing No. 0687), to ensure odour nuisance does not undermine the amenity of nearby residential premises.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;REASON:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;To ensure that the development does not result in odour nuisance to nearby residential properties and to protect the amenities of the area.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "<p>The Development hereby permitted shall only be carried out and completed strictly in accordance with the submitted plans hereby approved and any subsequent approval of details.\r\n</p><p><br></p><p>\r\nREASON: To ensure that the development hereby permitted is carried out in full accordance with the plans hereby approved.\r\n</p>",
    "<p>The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the expiration of three years beginning with the date of this permission.</p><p><br></p><p>\r\n</p><p>\r\nREASON: In order to comply with the provisions of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).</p><p>\r\n</p>",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;The applicant shall provide a scheme of sound insulation between the commercial premises on the ground floor and any adjoining residential premises that shall be submitted for approval to the Council’s Planning Team for approval. The proposed requirement is to achieve a minimum airborne sound insulation level of 55 dB DnTw+Ctr. The development shall not be occupied until the sound insulation scheme is approved and has been implemented in its entirety. Thereafter, the sound insulation scheme shall be maintained in perpetuity in accordance with the approved details.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;REASON:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-size: 14px;&quot;&gt;To ensure that the development does not result in odour nuisance to nearby residential properties and to protect the amenities of the area.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;color: rgb(34, 34, 34); font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: small;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
